A||N||4||Bigfieroman||Engine replaced, new engine problems?||||1||
Z||000000||Bigfieroman||07-20-2001||02:56 PM||||Well, the engine that I replaced mine with was running great in the other car, and now that it is in my car, my mechanic is running into problems.  He has told me that the engine resists revving up and misfires, and the only differences in the engine since it has ben put in my car is that I have changed the plug wires from stock to the splitfire 8mm wires sold by the Fiero Store, added K&N air and oil filters, and switched to Mobil 1 10w-30.  Could it be those wires?  He says there are no computer codes and there are no other problems.  Thanks a bunch all.<P>------------------<BR>I once got a warning from a Police officer because he couldn't keep up with me around some twisties.  the prerequisite for a warning instead of a ticket was that I must let him drive it back and forth the way we had come.  Burned a quater tank of my gas!||||reg||1
Z||000001||West Coast Fiero||07-20-2001||03:35 PM||||your problem sounds electrical. Check to see if all plug wires are attached, if so then these are signs of an ignition module and/or the coil going out<P>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||07-20-2001||03:36 PM||||did you change the engines computer too? yours may be bad. And its easy to swap a couple of plug wires, my Pontiac dealership mechanics did once.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 07-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||kslish||07-21-2001||01:22 AM||||Swap the wires back to the originals to see if that is the problem (doubt it though).   Otherwise, my money would be on the coil.  Failing ignition modules tend to only go completely (i.e. engine wont fire at all) or only act up when the car is warm, but are still fine when you first start the car.  <P>Love my MSD coil ($35 bucks from Summit)....cleared my occasional miss right up. <P>Also, double check the connections on the engine wire harness.  Something could have been cut or cracked or the connectors may not be completely on something.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Dan87GT||07-21-2001||06:02 AM||||Sounds like a plugged catalytic converter me||||reg||1
